<tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/120"><tei:pb n="468" ed="1949 shabbat/minchah" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n492_medium.jpg"/><tei:head xml:lang="en">Psalm 120</tei:head><tei:p><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/120/1"/>A Pilgrim Song. In my distress I called to the Lord, and he answered me. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/120/2"/>O Lord, save me from lying lips, from a deceitful tongue. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/120/3"/>What will a deceitful tongue give you, what will it profit you? <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/120/4"/>Sharp arrows of a warrior with burning coals of broom! <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/120/5"/>Woe is me that I dwell in Meshek, that I reside amid the tents of Kedar. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/120/6"/>Too long have I been living where men hate peace. <tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/120/7"/>I am all for peace; but when I speak, they are for war. <tei:milestone unit="verse"/></tei:p></tei:div>
